{number: 9}
{title: Come, Christians, Join to Sing}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Come, Christians, [Db] join to [Ab] sing
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
[Ab] Loud praise to [Db] Christ our [Ab] King;
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
Let [Ab] all, with [Eb] heart and voice,
Be-[Ab] fore His [Eb] throne rejoice;
[Ab] Praise is His [Db] gracious [Ab] choice:
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Come, lift your [Db] hearts on [Ab] high,
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
[Ab] Let praises [Db] fill the [Ab] sky;
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
He [Ab] is our [Eb] Guide and Friend;
To [Ab] us He’ll [Eb] condescend;
His [Ab] love shall [Db] never [Ab] end:
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Praise yet our [Db] Christ a-[Ab] gain,
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
[Ab] Life shall not [Db] end the [Ab] strain;
Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!
On [Ab] heaven’s [Eb] blissful shore
His [Ab] goodness [Eb] we’ll adore,
[Ab] Singing for-[Db] ever-[Ab] more,
“Alle-[Eb7] luia! A-[Ab] men!”
{end_of_verse}
